; Walk through a given exit (follow, enter, go into)
;
; Common end of the handlers #R$8FCD (verbs enter and go into: the first
; object is the place to go to) and #R$8FD6 (follow). They call #R$9F2D, which
; searches the exits of the current location for the one that leads to a
; wanted location. This routine refuses the command (#R$9F76) when no exit was
; found (A = $FF), when the exit has no destination, or when #R$8E85 says the
; obstacle or the destination stops the subject. Otherwise, when the command is
; really performed (#R$9D44), it makes the exit's direction the verb
; (CommandId), clears FirstObject and continues in the move handler at #R$8DAB,
; which does the walk as if the player had typed the compass direction.
; .
; #R$8E85 reads TakeId and TakeWeight, which only #R$8D9D sets, after the
; walk starts, so here they still have the values from the last move.
; .
; Hardware: none.
;
; A Result of #R$9F2D: $FF when no exit was found
; IX Exit record found (direction, obstacle, destination)
@label=WalkToExit
@isub=CP END_MARK
c$8F3E CP $FF        ;
 $8F40 JP Z,$9F76    ; no such exit
@isub=LD A,(IX+EXIT_DEST)
 $8F43 LD A,(IX+$02) ; destination
 $8F46 CP $00        ;
 $8F48 JP Z,$9F76    ;
@isub=LD A,(IX+EXIT_OBSTACLE)
 $8F4B LD A,(IX+$01) ; obstacle
 $8F4E PUSH IX       ;
 $8F50 CALL $8E85    ;
 $8F53 POP IX        ;
 $8F55 JP NZ,$9F76   ; blocked
 $8F58 CALL $9D44    ; only when really performing
 $8F5B LD A,(IX+$00) ; the exit's direction
 $8F5E LD ($B6E7),A  ; becomes the verb
@isub=LD A,AT_LOCATION
 $8F61 LD A,$FF      ;
 $8F63 LD ($B6E8),A  ; no first object
 $8F66 JP $8DAB      ; move
